  <middle>
    <section anchor="introduction" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-1">
      <name slugifiedName="name-introduction">Introduction</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-1">The E.164 to Uniform Resource Identifiers (URIs) <xref target="RFC3986" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC3986"/> Dynamic
Delegation Discovery System (DDDS) Application (ENUM) <xref target="RFC6116" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC6116"/>
transforms E.164 <xref target="E164" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="E164"/> numbers into URIs using the Domain Name
System (DNS) <xref target="RFC1035" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1035"/>.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-2">IAX (Inter-Asterisk eXchange) <xref target="RFC5456" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5456"/> is an &quot;all-in-one&quot; protocol
for handling multimedia in IP networks.  It combines both control and
media services in the same protocol.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-3">This document registers an Enumservice for the IAX <xref target="RFC5456" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5456"/> protocol
according to the guidelines given in <xref target="RFC6117" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC6117"/>.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="iana-registration" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2">
      <name slugifiedName="name-iana-registration">IANA Registration</name>
      <artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt="" pn="section-2-1"><![CDATA[
      <record>
       <!-- iax -->
       <class>Protocol-Based</class>
       <type>iax</type>
       <!-- No subtype -->
       <urischeme>iax</urischeme>
       <functionalspec>
         <paragraph>
           The 'iax' Enumservice is used to map E.164 numbers to
           IAX URIs.  Such URIs identify resources capable of being
           contacted to provide a communication session using the
           IAX protocol <xref target="RFC5456"/>.
         </paragraph>
         <paragraph>
           A client selecting this NAPTR needs to be able to support
           communication utilizing the IAX protocol.
         </paragraph>
       </functionalspec>
       <security>
         See <xref type="rfc" data="6315"/>, Section 4.
       </security>
       <usage>COMMON</usage>
       <registrationdocs>
         <xref type="rfc" data="6315"/>
       </registrationdocs>
       <requesters>
         <xref type="person" data="Ed_Guy"/>
         <xref type="person" data="Klaus_Darilion"/>
       </requesters>
     </record>

     <people>
       <person id="Ed_Guy">
